  "shortcutDescription": "Enable configurable shortcuts in the Profile section to quickly access your favorite sections in Torn",
  "shortcutEditDescription": "Adds a dedicated icon at the end of the Profile shortcuts list to open the editor quickly.",
  "clockDateDescription": "Add an extra row for the date wherever the TCT clock is shown. You can also specify the desired format (day/month or month/day)",
  "clockEventDescription": "If enabled, the TCT Clock will be highlighted whenever there is an event or competition active in Torn",
  "discreetScope": "Covers notifications created by Torn PDA on this phone and Torn PDA server alerts. Not covered: Torn private messages on iOS while the app is in the background or closed, other apps and the Torn website",
  "clearNotificationsDescription": "This will remove all Torn PDA notifications from your notifications bar when you launch the app. Deactivate it if you prefer to clear them manually.",
  "vibrationDescription": "This vibration applies to automatic alerts while the app is active or in the background.",
  "alarmClockDescription": "Applies to manually activated alarms in all sections (Travel, Loot, Profile, etc.). Some Android clock apps have issues with multiple timers or distinguishing between sound and vibration. If you experience issues, consider installing ",
  "googleClock": "Google's Clock application",
  "alarmListDescription": "These are the alarms scheduled by Torn PDA. On iOS they are handled directly by the app.\n\nYou can clear them here if you no longer need them.",
  "compactWidgetDescription": "By default, the short, one-row layout accommodates a couple of shortcuts by sacrificing chaining information and moving the reload icon to the top. Enabling this option removes shortcuts to free up space for the chaining bar",
  "cooldownWidgetDescription": "If enabled, a tap on any cooldown icon will launch the app and browser to your personal or faction items. Otherwise, the remaining cooldown time is displayed. NOTE: you may need to try a couple of times after switching for the widget to update properly.",
  "racingWidgetDescription": "If enabled, tapping the racing icon will open the racing page in the browser. Otherwise, the racing status text is displayed.  NOTE: you may need to try a couple of times after switching for the widget to update properly.",
  "spiesDescription": "Choose the source of spied stats. This affects the stats shown when you visit a profile in the browser, as well as those shown in the War section (Chaining)",
  "mixedSourcesDescription": "Whilst enabled, if a target's spy info cannot be found in the preferred source, it will also be taken from the other source if available. Switching sources preserves info unless the new source also contains a spy for the target.",
  "deleteSpiesDescription": "Deletes all spies information from the local database if you prefer not to use spies info or if there is an issue with the downloaded stats.",
  "playerNotesDescription": "View and edit all your player notes, including those from targets, friends, stakeouts, and war members.",
  "scouterDescription": "Enable FFScouter battle stats estimations in player profiles, war/retal cards and the FFScouter tab in the Chaining section",
  "scouterNotesDescription": "Shows the personal and faction notes stored in FFScouter in the notes dialog, and a counter next to the notes of war, target and profile cards",
  "preferredNotesDescription": "When a player has both a Torn PDA note and FFScouter notes, cards show this one. Tap the notebook icon to open your Torn PDA note, or the FFS counter to open the FFScouter ones",
  "bountyBoardDescription": "Shows the Bounty Board tab in the FFScouter section of Chaining, where you can hit the players with a bounty on them and place your own",
  "battleScoreDescription": "When enabled, war/retal cards and profile checks will show the FFScouter battle score estimate (~12.5M) instead of the vague range (2M-25M) for unspied targets. Disabling this clears the cache.",
  "staleSpiesDescription": "When set, FFS will replace spied stats on cards if the spy is older than the selected number of months. Sorting, filters, and SmartScore will also use FFS in that case.",
  "yataEstimateDescription": "Enable YATA stats estimations in sections where spied or estimated stats are shown (e.g.: war targets cards, retal cards or profile widget)",
  "nerveSourceDescription": "Choose the source of the Natural Nerve Bar (NNB) that will be shown for each member of your faction available to plan an organized crime",
  "organizedCrimesDescription": "Torn PDA will try to identify if your faction has changed to OC v2. If you would like to remain in OC v1 (e.g.: if you join an OC1 faction), revert back by using this toggle",
  "revivingDescription": "Choose which reviving services you might want to use. If enabled, when you are in hospital you'll have the option to call one of their revivers from several places (e.g., Profile and Chaining sections).",
  "rotationDescription": "If enabled, the interface will rotate from portrait to landscape if the device is rotated. Be aware that landscape might not be comfortable on narrow mobile devices.",
  "splitScreenDescription": "If enabled, the device screen will be split to show the main app and the browser simultaneously. A minimum width of 800 dpi is required.",
  "splitRotationDescription": "Allow auto rotation to use split screen on phones and foldables",
  "splitExitDescription": "When split screen is no longer active (e.g., device rotated to a width lower than 800 dpi), this option determines whether the webview or the app remains in the foreground.",
  "splitLinksDescription": "When the app and a browser are side by side, links tapped in the app open in the current tab or a new tab of the browser next to it, or on the app's side, which then shows the tab it was covering or a new one",
  "refreshRateDescription": "Enables the highest available refresh rate on supported devices (e.g., 90Hz, 120Hz). May increase battery consumption and device heat but provides smoother animations.\n\nNOTE: it might be necessary to restart the app after disabling this feature.",
  "themeDescription": "Please note that the main theme selector switch is located in the drawer menu of Torn PDA. Here you will be able to select other theming options",
  "darkThemeDescription": "Specifies which dark theme is activated when the web or device switches to dark mode",
  "accessibleColorsDescription": "Replaces colored texts with the default color for improved accessibility; applies only to the app, not the web.",
  "dynamicIconDescription": "Allows Torn PDA to change the main app icon based on certain conditions",
  "overrideIconDescription": "By using this option, you can manually trigger (some) app icons even if the conditions are not met",
  "statusCounterDescription": "Shows a player status counter attached to the Torn PDA icon in the main app sections and in the browser three-dotted icon, whenever the player is hospitalised, jailed or traveling",
  "appBarDescription": "Note: this will affect other quick access items such as the quick crimes bar in the browser",
  "backButtonDescription": "This will only have effect on certain devices, depending on your configuration. Dictates how to proceed when the app detects a back button press or swipe that would otherwise close the app. Note: in the browser, the back button always triggers backwards navigation",
  "updateDialogDescription": "Disable the dialog that notifies you about new PDA versions and features when the app starts",
  "alternativeKeyDescription": "Use this section to configure alternative API keys for the external partners that Torn PDA connects with. CAUTION: ensure these other keys are working correctly, as Torn PDA is unable to check for errors and certain sections may stop working",
  "apiRateDescription": "Enables a small progress bar on top of Torn PDA's logo in the main drawer menu, with real-time count of the number of API calls performed in the last minute",
  "apiRateWarningDescription": "If enabled, a quick message will be shown when approaching (95 calls in 60 seconds) the maximum API call rate. This message will be then inhibited for 30 seconds",
  "apiDelayDescription": "Artificially delay API calls above 95 in 60 seconds to avoid hitting the max API rate. If enabled, the current queue information will be shown in the main drawer menu API bar. NOTE: this option cannot take into account API calls generated outside of Torn PDA",
  "inventoryDescription": "If enabled, your inventory is loaded as soon as you open Items or Foreign Stocks. Torn serves inventory by item category, one API call each (up to 25 in Items), cached for an hour. If disabled, inventory is only loaded when you tap the box icon in those sections",
  "backupDisabled": "Online backup is temporarily disabled, please check in game or Discord for more information",
  "backupSettingsDescription": "This will allow you to backup your main app settings (e.g.: scripts, shortcuts, etc.) locally so that you can later restore them if needed or share them across different devices",
  "restoreDescription": "This will download your saved settings and restore them in the app. Please be aware that this will overwrite your current preferences",
  "shareDescription": "This will allow you to share your settings and receive settings from other players using the player ID and a password",
  "clearBackupDescription": "In case there is an issue with your online backup when restoring or if you simply want to clear it, this will delete the online saved data",
  "drawerMemoryDescription": "This will show a small memory usage bar on below the Torn PDA's logo in the main drawer menu, with real-time count of the app's memory usage",
  "browserMemoryDescription": "This will show an icon in the browser's appbar with which you can toggle real-time information of the app's memory usage where the page title normally goes",
  "defaultStyleOnly": "NOTE: this option only works in the 'default' browser style. If have currently selected a different style!",
  "testApiDescription": "In case you are facing connection problems, this will ping Torn's API and show whether it is reachable from your device. If it isn't, it might be due to your DNS servers (try switching from WiFi to mobile data).",
  "errorLogDescription": "If you ever need to inspect recent API failures (v1 or v2), open the error history here.",
  "debugMessagesDescription": "Enable specific debug messages for app failure testing. This is an advanced feature that may generate extra error messages; do not use unless requested.",
  "resetTutorialDescription": "This will clear all the app's tutorial pop-ups so you can review them again. Note that some tutorials (e.g., those in the browser) require an app restart to fully reset.",
  "resetChainingDescription": "This will reset all your War/Chaining sorting preferences, smart score weights, and filters to their default values.",
  "chainingFiltersDescription": "If you experience issues with sorting or filters in the War page, use this button to restore default values.",
  "apiUse": "Torn PDA needs your API Key to obtain your user's information. The key is protected in the app and will not be shared under any circumstances.",
  "apiTerms": "See how we comply with Torn's Terms of Service",
  "apiTermsHint": "Expand the section below to see how Torn PDA complies with these guidelines.",
  "apiStorage": "Persistent - until you remove the key from the app. This also applies to the Torn PDA server",
  "apiSharing": "Your data is not shared. Only service owners may access data for maintenance and support purposes",
  "apiPurpose": "To provide application features and display your Torn data within the app",
  "apiKeyStorage": "Stored remotely and securely. Used only for automated requests to the Torn API on your behalf",
  "apiPrivacy": "Note: if you are curious about Torn PDA's own privacy policy, you can access it in the Abour section of the app",
  "apiInstructions": "\nYou can get your API key in the Torn website by tapping your profile picture (upper right corner) and going to Settings, API Keys. Torn PDA only needs a Limited Access key.\n",
  "apiProtect": "\nIn any case, please make sure to follow Torn's staff recommendations on how to protect your key from any malicious use.",
  "apiRemove": "\nYou can always remove it from the app or reset it in your Torn preferences page.",
